;; lower-check's negative controls (doc/GATE-SURVEY.md, GTS81 (a); arbace.cpp.check's judge, control-result): beside the known
;; file the judge is given. The judge compares the subject's lowered run (low.status, low.out, low.err) with the reference's
;; original run (orig.*) by the run's own comparison (run-verdict), and fails when they are the same (the comparison passes what
;; differs) or when the reference, in the run, has no original run. A control whose subject or reference is not in the run's
;; list, or whose run is not comparable, is left. No file or run of its own: two samples of the samples list, both passing
;; (test/cpp/lower-results.edn), with other outputs. No control is a row of results.tsv, summary.edn or the counts.
;; Since CX8 the run checks' controls too, :level :run (lower-check leaves them): bin/cppi check's and check --aot's judge
;; (arbace.cpp.check/run-judge, run-result) judges the subject's node and run against the reference's g++ run
;; (test/cpp/ref-gxx15.edn), which must not pass; one whose subject is not in the run, not built or not run is left. Read with
;; the Clojure reader.
[{:id "_control/bitfields-vs-io" :subject "samples/bitfields.cpp" :reference "samples/io.cpp"
  :why "status 0 both, bitfields' 43 bytes of output against io's 6 (differs)"}
 {:id "_control/run/bitfields-vs-io" :level :run :subject "samples/bitfields.cpp" :reference "samples/io.cpp"
  :why "bin/cppi check's judge: bitfields' run on ci (status 0, 43 bytes) against io's g++ run (status 0, 6 bytes): differ stdout"}
 ;; cppi-check (2026-11-05): the sampling's control (bin/cppi check --corpus gxx-dg-run --sample 25, and --aot), both programs in the
 ;; sampling and passing (test/cpp/check-every-25-linux-amd64.edn)
 {:id "_control/run/no-elide2-vs-io" :level :run :subject "gxx-dg-run/init/no-elide2.C" :reference "samples/io.cpp"
  :why "bin/cppi check's judge: no-elide2's run (status 0, 15 bytes: ctor lines) against io.cpp's g++ run (status 0, 6 bytes: io has no verdict of its own, so g++'s run is its reference; cpp-90: dr2137-1, the reference before, is judged by its own verdict, exit 0, which no-elide2 meets): differ stdout"}

 ;; cpp-90 (2026-11-07): the token check's controls (arbace.repr.cpp.ppcheck/controls; bin/repr-cpp pp-check, the essential subset holds
 ;; both files): the subject's port judged by the level's own judgment against the reference's recorded answer must differ
 {:id "_control/pp/udl-vs-prefixes" :level :pp :subject "cpp-lexical/udl.cpp" :reference "cpp-lexical/prefixes.cpp"
  :why "udl.cpp's preprocessed stream's digest against prefixes.cpp's g++ -E -P digest (test/repr/cpp/pp-gxx.sha256): both agree with their own"}
 {:id "_control/lex/udl-vs-prefixes" :level :lex :subject "cpp-lexical/udl.cpp" :reference "cpp-lexical/prefixes.cpp"
  :why "udl.cpp's raw tokens' digest against prefixes.cpp's clang raw tokens (test/repr/cpp/lex-clang.sha256)"}
 ;; the dg check's control (arbace.repr.cpp.dg/controls; bin/repr-cpp dg, the dg-error part): both files pass on their own directives
 {:id "_control/dg/dr2082-vs-dr1423" :level :dg :subject "gxx-dg/DRs/dr2082.C" :reference "gxx-dg/DRs/dr1423.C"
  :why "dr2082's read (an error at line 9) judged against dr1423's dg-error lines (4 and 7): missed and extra"}
